-- CONTROL for #1647 — main.mdk with ONE dimension flipped: the two same-spelled
-- interfaces now declare `speak` at the SAME signature. Everything else stands:
-- two modules, two interfaces both spelled `Speak`, two methods both spelled
-- `speak`, two impls, the same `build` verb (so the same front end, the same
-- emitter, the same clang, the same link). It must build at exit 0.
--
-- Per #1144 a control is graded on its EXIT CODE ONLY, and this control's verb is
-- `build`, whose exit code is the emitter's — which is precisely the channel the
-- pin blames. A red here says the EMIT path broke in general (CONTROL-BROKE), not
-- that #1647 was fixed.
import ctla.{useA}
import ctlb.{useB}

main =
  let _ = println useA
  println useB
